# ABP Unit of Work

## Automatic Unit of Work
ABP automatically manages unit of work for:
- Application service methods
- Controller actions
- Repository operations

## Manual Unit of Work
```csharp
public class MyService : ITransientDependency
{
    private readonly IUnitOfWorkManager _unitOfWorkManager;

    public async Task DoWorkAsync()
    {
        using var uow = _unitOfWorkManager.Begin();
        
        // Do work...
        
        await uow.CompleteAsync();
    }
}
```

## SaveChanges Behavior
```csharp
[UnitOfWork(IsDisabled = true)] // Disable auto UoW
public async Task MyMethodAsync() { }

[UnitOfWork(IsolationLevel = IsolationLevel.Serializable)]
public async Task HighIsolationMethodAsync() { }
```

## Best Practice
- Always call `UpdateAsync` explicitly on repositories
- Don't rely on automatic change tracking
- Use `[UnitOfWork]` attribute for non-service methods that need transaction
